IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `wa-interpretation-time`
IMPORT `wa-seat`

-- Worked cases for the seat layer (wa-seat.l4): a person who has a time limit to meet under a Western Australian Act, or who needs
-- to know when something takes effect.  One case at least per question, with the facts such a person would state, and cases outside
-- the encoding (NOTHING).  Every expected value is written from the Act's text before the run; a failing assertion would be a
-- finding, never an edit of the expected value.
-- Weekdays, by hand calendar arithmetic: 1 Jan 2025 is a Wednesday, so Sat 4 Jan, Sun 5 Jan, Mon 6 Jan, Tue 7 Jan, Sat 15 Feb,
-- Mon 17 Feb, Tue 18 Feb, Sat 1 Mar, Mon 3 Mar, Sun 9 Mar, Mon 10 Mar, Tue 11 Mar, Wed 12 Mar, Sun 30 Mar, Mon 31 Mar 2025;
-- 1 Jan 2026 is a Thursday, so Sat 31 Jan, Sun 1 Feb, Mon 2 Feb, Tue 3 Feb, Sat 28 Feb, Sun 1 Mar, Mon 2 Mar 2026;
-- Thu 29 Feb 2024; Sun 16 Jul 2028, Mon 17 Jul 2028; Tue 15 Jan 2030; Sun 1 Sep 2030, Mon 2 Sep 2030.
-- An unused date is written 1 Jan 2000.

§ `Cases -- the seat of a person who has a time limit`

§§ `Coming into operation`

-- s 20(2): assent on or after 1 July 1984, the Act names no day: the 28th day after the day of assent.  10 March + 28 days = 7 April.
#ASSERT `On which day does an Act come into operation` FALSE (Date 10 3 2025) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) FALSE EQUALS JUST (Date 7 4 2025)
-- s 20(1): assent before 1 July 1984: the day of assent.
#ASSERT `On which day does an Act come into operation` FALSE (Date 30 6 1984) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) FALSE EQUALS JUST (Date 30 6 1984)
-- the Act names its own day
#ASSERT `On which day does an Act come into operation` FALSE (Date 10 3 2025) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) TRUE (Date 1 9 2025) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) FALSE EQUALS JUST (Date 1 9 2025)
-- s 20(3): reserved on or after 1 July 1984: the day the assent is proclaimed, and nothing until it is
#ASSERT `On which day does an Act come into operation` TRUE (Date 10 3 2025) TRUE (Date 2 6 2025) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) FALSE EQUALS JUST (Date 2 6 2025)
#ASSERT `On which day does an Act come into operation` TRUE (Date 10 3 2025) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- reserved before 1 July 1984: the section does not say
#ASSERT `On which day does an Act come into operation` TRUE (Date 1 6 1984) TRUE (Date 1 8 1984) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- the Act leaves the day to proclamation: no day until one is fixed
#ASSERT `On which day does an Act come into operation` FALSE (Date 10 3 2025) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) TRUE (Date 1 1 2000) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `On which day does an Act come into operation` FALSE (Date 10 3 2025) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) TRUE (Date 1 12 2025) TRUE EQUALS JUST (Date 1 12 2025)

-- s 21: in operation from the beginning of the first day
#ASSERT `Is the law already in operation at a given hour of its first day` (Date 1 7 2025) (Date 1 7 2025) 0
#ASSERT `Is the law already in operation at a given hour of its first day` (Date 1 7 2025) (Date 1 7 2025) 17
#ASSERT NOT (`Is the law already in operation at a given hour of its first day` (Date 1 7 2025) (Date 30 6 2025) 23)

-- s 25(3): the notice takes effect no earlier than the commencement day
#ASSERT `On which day does a notice or instrument made early take effect` (Date 1 7 2025) (Date 1 6 2025) EQUALS Date 1 7 2025
#ASSERT `On which day does a notice or instrument made early take effect` (Date 1 7 2025) (Date 15 8 2025) EQUALS Date 15 8 2025

§§ `Repeal`

-- s 35: the old provision lasts to the end of the day before its replacement begins
#ASSERT `Is the old provision still in operation on a given day` (Date 30 6 2025) (Date 1 7 2025)
#ASSERT NOT (`Is the old provision still in operation on a given day` (Date 1 7 2025) (Date 1 7 2025))

§§ `Subsidiary legislation`

-- s 41(1)(b): the day of publication, or the day the legislation names
#ASSERT `On which day does subsidiary legislation come into operation` (Date 2 4 2025) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) EQUALS Date 2 4 2025
#ASSERT `On which day does subsidiary legislation come into operation` (Date 2 4 2025) TRUE (Date 1 5 2025) EQUALS Date 1 5 2025

-- s 42(2)
#ASSERT `Have the regulations that affect me ceased to have effect` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `Have the regulations that affect me ceased to have effect` FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Have the regulations that affect me ceased to have effect` FALSE FALSE)
-- s 42(4): 7 days from 10 April expire on 17 April; they take effect on 18 April
#ASSERT `On which day do the amended or substituted regulations take effect` (Date 10 4 2025) EQUALS Date 18 4 2025
-- s 42(6)
#ASSERT `On which day are the earlier regulations revived` TRUE TRUE (Date 10 6 2025) (Date 20 3 2025) EQUALS JUST (Date 10 6 2025)
#ASSERT `On which day are the earlier regulations revived` FALSE TRUE (Date 1 1 2000) (Date 20 3 2025) EQUALS JUST (Date 21 3 2025)
#ASSERT `On which day are the earlier regulations revived` TRUE FALSE (Date 10 6 2025) (Date 20 3 2025) EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 43(6)
#ASSERT `What is the most I can be fined under a regulation, rule, local law or bylaw` (Date 1 3 2025) FALSE EQUALS JUST 1000
#ASSERT `What is the most I can be fined under a regulation, rule, local law or bylaw` (Date 30 6 1984) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `What is the most I can be fined under a regulation, rule, local law or bylaw` (Date 1 3 2025) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `Decisions that affect me`

-- s 48A: on a Sunday (5 January 2025) a court document may be served
#ASSERT `May a court document be served on me on a weekend or public holiday` (Date 5 1 2025) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `May a court document be served on me on a weekend or public holiday` (Date 5 1 2025) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 49
#ASSERT `Can a person who is only acting in the office make the decision` `the person for the time being lawfully holding the office` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can a person who is only acting in the office make the decision` `a person acting in the office` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can a person who is only acting in the office make the decision` `a person performing the functions of the office` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can a person who is only acting in the office make the decision` `a person who is none of these` EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 51
#ASSERT `Is the authority free to refuse my application` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is the authority free to refuse my application` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Can I still appeal against or seek a review of a refusal` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I still appeal against or seek a review of a refusal` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 54(2): five members provided for, so a quorum is 3; 5 present and 3 agree: valid.  2 present: no quorum.  5 present, 2 agree: no majority.
-- Four provided for, quorum 2; 4 present, 2 agree: 2 is not more than half of 4.  Two provided for: the rule does not reach.
#ASSERT `Was the board's decision validly made by the members at the meeting` 5 3 5 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Was the board's decision validly made by the members at the meeting` 2 2 5 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Was the board's decision validly made by the members at the meeting` 5 2 5 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Was the board's decision validly made by the members at the meeting` 4 2 4 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Was the board's decision validly made by the members at the meeting` 2 2 2 EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 57
#ASSERT `Is the decision of the body invalid because of a vacancy or an irregularity` `a vacancy in the membership of the body` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Is the decision of the body invalid because of a vacancy or an irregularity` `a minor irregularity in the convening or conduct of a meeting` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Is the decision of the body invalid because of a vacancy or an irregularity` `a major irregularity in the convening or conduct of a meeting` EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `Counting my time`

-- The seven worked cases.  "From" a day: the day itself does not count (s 61(1)(b)); a month is a calendar month (s 62); an end on an
-- excluded day moves to the next day that is not one (s 61(1)(e)).
-- 1. three years from 16 July 2025: first day 17 July 2025, 36 months, ends 16 July 2028 (a Sunday), so Monday 17 July 2028
#ASSERT `What is the last day I have to do it` 3 `in years` `is reckoned from or after the day` (Date 16 7 2025) EMPTY EMPTY EQUALS JUST (Date 17 7 2028)
#ASSERT `What is the last day of my period by the calendar` 3 `in years` `is reckoned from or after the day` (Date 16 7 2025) EQUALS JUST (Date 16 7 2028)
-- 2. five years from 15 January 2025: ends 15 January 2030 (a Tuesday)
#ASSERT `What is the last day I have to do it` 5 `in years` `is reckoned from or after the day` (Date 15 1 2025) EMPTY EMPTY EQUALS JUST (Date 15 1 2030)
-- 3. five years from 1 September 2025: first day 2 September; ends 1 September 2030 (a Sunday), so Monday 2 September 2030
#ASSERT `What is the last day I have to do it` 5 `in years` `is reckoned from or after the day` (Date 1 9 2025) EMPTY EMPTY EQUALS JUST (Date 2 9 2030)
#ASSERT `What is the last day of my period by the calendar` 5 `in years` `is reckoned from or after the day` (Date 1 9 2025) EQUALS JUST (Date 1 9 2030)
-- 4. thirty days from 1 January 2026: first day 2 January, the 30th day is 31 January (a Saturday), so Monday 2 February 2026
#ASSERT `What is the last day I have to do it` 30 `in days` `is reckoned from or after the day` (Date 1 1 2026) EMPTY EMPTY EQUALS JUST (Date 2 2 2026)
#ASSERT `What is the last day of my period by the calendar` 30 `in days` `is reckoned from or after the day` (Date 1 1 2026) EQUALS JUST (Date 31 1 2026)
-- the same with Monday 2 February 2026 a public holiday: Tuesday 3 February (the holiday list may be either kind)
#ASSERT `What is the last day I have to do it` 30 `in days` `is reckoned from or after the day` (Date 1 1 2026) (LIST (Date 2 2 2026)) EMPTY EQUALS JUST (Date 3 2 2026)
#ASSERT `What is the last day I have to do it` 30 `in days` `is reckoned from or after the day` (Date 1 1 2026) EMPTY (LIST (Date 2 2 2026)) EQUALS JUST (Date 3 2 2026)
-- 5. two months from 31 December 2025: first day 1 January 2026, ends 28 February 2026 (a Saturday), so Monday 2 March 2026
#ASSERT `What is the last day I have to do it` 2 `in months` `is reckoned from or after the day` (Date 31 12 2025) EMPTY EMPTY EQUALS JUST (Date 2 3 2026)
#ASSERT `What is the last day of my period by the calendar` 2 `in months` `is reckoned from or after the day` (Date 31 12 2025) EQUALS JUST (Date 28 2 2026)
-- 6. one month from 31 January 2024: first day 1 February, ends 29 February 2024 (a Thursday)
#ASSERT `What is the last day I have to do it` 1 `in months` `is reckoned from or after the day` (Date 31 1 2024) EMPTY EMPTY EQUALS JUST (Date 29 2 2024)
-- 7. one year from 29 February 2024: first day 1 March 2024, ends 28 February 2025 (a Friday)
#ASSERT `What is the last day I have to do it` 1 `in years` `is reckoned from or after the day` (Date 29 2 2024) EMPTY EMPTY EQUALS JUST (Date 28 2 2025)
-- a period that begins on the named day: 28 days beginning on Monday 3 March 2025 end on Sunday 30 March, so Monday 31 March
#ASSERT `What is the last day I have to do it` 28 `in days` `begins at, on or with the day` (Date 3 3 2025) EMPTY EMPTY EQUALS JUST (Date 31 3 2025)
-- weeks: the Act does not mention them, so there is no answer
#ASSERT `What is the last day I have to do it` 4 `in weeks` `is reckoned from or after the day` (Date 3 3 2025) EMPTY EMPTY EQUALS NOTHING
-- the first day that counts
#ASSERT `What is the first day that counts in my period` 30 `in days` `is reckoned from or after the day` (Date 1 1 2026) EQUALS JUST (Date 2 1 2026)
#ASSERT `What is the first day that counts in my period` 30 `in days` `begins at, on or with the day` (Date 1 1 2026) EQUALS JUST (Date 1 1 2026)
-- am I in time? thirty days from 1 January 2026 end on Monday 2 February; the 3rd is too late unless Monday 2nd is a holiday
#ASSERT `Am I in time if I do it on a given day` (Date 2 2 2026) 30 `in days` `is reckoned from or after the day` (Date 1 1 2026) EMPTY EMPTY EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Am I in time if I do it on a given day` (Date 3 2 2026) 30 `in days` `is reckoned from or after the day` (Date 1 1 2026) EMPTY EMPTY EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Am I in time if I do it on a given day` (Date 3 2 2026) 30 `in days` `is reckoned from or after the day` (Date 1 1 2026) (LIST (Date 2 2 2026)) EMPTY EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Am I in time if I do it on a given day` (Date 3 2 2026) 4 `in weeks` `is reckoned from or after the day` (Date 1 1 2026) EMPTY EMPTY EQUALS NOTHING
-- which of my days count: Saturday 4 January 2025, Monday 6 January 2025 (ordinary, public holiday, public service holiday)
#ASSERT `Is this day an excluded day` (Date 4 1 2025) EMPTY EMPTY
#ASSERT NOT (`Is this day an excluded day` (Date 6 1 2025) EMPTY EMPTY)
#ASSERT `Is this day an excluded day` (Date 6 1 2025) (LIST (Date 6 1 2025)) EMPTY
#ASSERT `Is this day an excluded day` (Date 6 1 2025) EMPTY (LIST (Date 6 1 2025))
-- the day set for me is Saturday 4 January 2025: Monday 6th; Tuesday 7th if Monday is a holiday; an ordinary day is itself
#ASSERT `The day set for me is an excluded day: the latest day I can act` (Date 4 1 2025) EMPTY EMPTY EQUALS Date 6 1 2025
#ASSERT `The day set for me is an excluded day: the latest day I can act` (Date 4 1 2025) (LIST (Date 6 1 2025)) EMPTY EQUALS Date 7 1 2025
#ASSERT `The day set for me is an excluded day: the latest day I can act` (Date 7 1 2025) EMPTY EMPTY EQUALS Date 7 1 2025
-- within 7 days before Wednesday 12 March 2025: the time does not include the 12th, so the last day is Tuesday 11 March
#ASSERT `What is the last day I can act if I must do it within a number of days before a day` 7 (Date 12 3 2025) EMPTY EMPTY EQUALS JUST (Date 11 3 2025)
-- before Monday 10 March 2025 the day before is Sunday 9th; s 61(1)(e) read as written moves it to Monday 10th (see fork F3 in NOTES.md)
#ASSERT `What is the last day I can act if I must do it within a number of days before a day` 7 (Date 10 3 2025) EMPTY EMPTY EQUALS JUST (Date 10 3 2025)
-- days between two events: 1 and 15 March 2025
#ASSERT `How many days are there between the two events` `clear days` (Date 1 3 2025) (Date 15 3 2025) EQUALS 13
#ASSERT `How many days are there between the two events` `at least or not less than a number of days` (Date 1 3 2025) (Date 15 3 2025) EQUALS 13
#ASSERT `How many days are there between the two events` `a number of days not expressed in either of those ways` (Date 1 3 2025) (Date 15 3 2025) EQUALS 14
-- s 63
#ASSERT `If the law fixes no time must I act with all convenient speed` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`If the law fixes no time must I act with all convenient speed` TRUE)
-- s 64
#ASSERT `May I ask for more time after my time has run out` TRUE (Date 1 1 2025) FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `May I ask for more time after my time has run out` FALSE (Date 1 1 2025) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `May I ask for more time after my time has run out` TRUE (Date 30 6 1984) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `May I ask for more time after my time has run out` TRUE (Date 1 1 2025) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `If I do not do it`

-- s 71: convicted Monday 6 January 2025, still not done on Friday 10th: further offences on 7, 8, 9 and 10 January
#ASSERT `How many further offences am I guilty of` (Date 6 1 2025) (Date 10 1 2025) EQUALS 4
#ASSERT `How many further offences am I guilty of` (Date 6 1 2025) (Date 6 1 2025) EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `How much is the penalty for each further offence` FALSE 0 EQUALS 50
#ASSERT `How much is the penalty for each further offence` TRUE 200 EQUALS 200

§§ `Forms and documents`

-- s 74
#ASSERT `Does a small mistake in the prescribed form I used make it invalid` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Does a small mistake in the prescribed form I used make it invalid` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Does a small mistake in the prescribed form I used make it invalid` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 75(1): the day the letter would have arrived, unless the contrary is proved
#ASSERT `On which day is a document sent by post taken to be served` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE (Date 14 3 2025) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) EQUALS JUST (Date 14 3 2025)
#ASSERT `On which day is a document sent by post taken to be served` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE (Date 14 3 2025) TRUE (Date 18 3 2025) EQUALS JUST (Date 18 3 2025)
#ASSERT `On which day is a document sent by post taken to be served` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE (Date 14 3 2025) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 75(2), (3)
#ASSERT `May a document that must be served by registered post be sent by certified mail instead` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `May a document that must be served by registered post be sent by certified mail instead` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `May a document that must be served by registered post be sent by certified mail instead` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 76
#ASSERT `May a document be served on me in this way` `delivering the document to the person personally` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `May a document be served on me in this way` `leaving it at the person's usual or last known place of abode` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `May a document be served on me in this way` `leaving it at the usual or last known place of business of a person who is a principal of a business` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `May a document be served on me in this way` `leaving it at the usual or last known place of business of a person who is a principal of a business` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `May a document be served on me in this way` `delivering, leaving or posting it, addressed to a corporation or association, at its principal place of business or principal office in the State` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `May a document be served on me in this way` `delivering the document to the person personally` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `May a document be served on me in this way` `some other manner` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `Old Acts that adopt the Second Schedule of the 1918 Act`

-- B: one month after an offence on Wednesday 15 January 2025: the month ends Saturday 15 February, so Monday 17 February
#ASSERT `By which day must the complaint be made and the proceedings started` `section B -- one month` (Date 15 1 2025) EMPTY EMPTY EQUALS JUST (Date 17 2 2025)
#ASSERT `By which day must the complaint be made and the proceedings started` `section B -- one month` (Date 15 1 2025) (LIST (Date 17 2 2025)) EMPTY EQUALS JUST (Date 18 2 2025)
-- C, D, E: three, six and twelve months after the same offence
#ASSERT `By which day must the complaint be made and the proceedings started` `section C -- three months` (Date 15 1 2025) EMPTY EMPTY EQUALS JUST (Date 15 4 2025)
#ASSERT `By which day must the complaint be made and the proceedings started` `section D -- six months` (Date 15 1 2025) EMPTY EMPTY EQUALS JUST (Date 15 7 2025)
#ASSERT `By which day must the complaint be made and the proceedings started` `section E -- twelve months` (Date 15 1 2025) EMPTY EMPTY EQUALS JUST (Date 15 1 2026)
